   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lack of connectivity is a major restraint on growth in South Asia. But having options in infrastructure means countries can exercise agency. The South Asia Regional Infrastructure and Connectivity (SARIC) program has provided technical assistance and training to design and fund a pipeline of transport and energy projects. SARIC has provided technical support to the Public Private Authority of Bangladesh and Chittagong Port Authority (CPA) on due diligence, design, and negotiation of a private sector concession for operation of the Patenga Container Terminal. Signed in December 2023, the agreement supports Bangladesh&#x2019;s first private sector&#x2013;run port terminal. SARIC has also supported Bangladesh in making regulatory changes which improve efficiency in the port handling 92% of the country&#x2019;s seaborne trade.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
